  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rApplication Form,\rDesign & Access Statement,\rP100 Rev R1 (Existing Floor Plans),\rP101 Rev R1 (Proposed Floor Plans),\rP102 Rev R1 (Existing Block Plan),\rP103 Rev R1 (Proposed Block Plan),\rP104 (Bin Storage Details),\rP104 (Bike Storage Details),\rP106 Rev R1 (Location Plan).\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning. \r",
    "Notwithstanding the details shown on the approved drawings, the development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until a cycle store with the capability of accommodating at least one cycle has been fully constructed on site, the cycle store shall be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rThe siting and proportions of the cycle store shall be in accordance with details shown within Drawing No. P103 Rev R1 (Proposed Block Plan) and P104 (Bike Storage Details), however the cycle store shall be configured to ensure that the doors not open onto the public highway along Walton Street\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rThe bin store shall be configured to ensure that the doors not open onto the public highway along Walton Street\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of future occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices, and support borough-wide recycling targets.\r"
  ],
